From 40faa10c8abdee3d86ff17bb4717787e43fd6bd7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: exeroom536 <352890649+exeroom536@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 10:04:16 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 29/33] super-amd: dedicated hot spares

AMD volumes can have up to four spares of their own, taken before the
global ones.  With the subarray_spare method:

- mdadm <volume> --add-spare <disk> assigns a disk of the container as a
  dedicated hot spare of the volume (a global spare loses that role, in
  the configuration and its label), --remove unassigns it;
- --remove of a spare from the container unassigns its roles (mdmon
  records it, or mdadm itself when mdmon does not run for the
  container);
- mdmon rebuilds onto a volume's own dedicated spares first, in the
  order of its list (the AMD driver's order), from any controller; a
  dedicated spare taken leaves the list.

A disk is taken as the AMD core takes one: an online RAID disk, not in
the volume, with room for a member's extent.

Written by Claude Opus 5.5 and Claude Fable 5.2, AI models by Anthropic.
---
